      "summary": "The npm source checker can pass when one lockfile package has an approved URL but another installable package has no `resolved` URL. With a custom registry configured, `npm ci` can fetch that package from an unapproved source.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/ci/check-sources.mjs",
          "line": 21,
          "message": "A08:2025 — Reject installable lockfile entries without an approved resolved URL, or validate the configured npm registry too; otherwise npm can fetch packages from an unapproved registry.",
          "confidence": 0.84,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The checker validates only string-valued `resolved` fields and passes if it finds at least one. It does not reject package entries without `resolved` or validate the npm registry configured in `.npmrc`; npm can fetch such entries from that registry.",
            "failureScenario": "A pull request sets `frontend/.npmrc` to an attacker-controlled registry and adds a lockfile package entry without `resolved`, while another entry has an approved npmjs.org URL. The checker passes, then `npm ci` can fetch the unresolved package from the attacker-controlled registry (OWASP A08:2025)."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
